      "writtenOn": "2026-07-28T22:27:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1) Regarding the race: yeah, as you mentioned, I think it can\u0027t happen\n\n2) Regarding the suggested code change, do you rather mean:\n```\n--- a/arch/x86/kvm/vmx/vmx.c\n+++ b/arch/x86/kvm/vmx/vmx.c\n@@ -9358,7 +9358,10 @@ __init int vmx_hardware_setup(void)\n        store_idt(\u0026dt);\n        host_idt_base \u003d dt.address;\n \n-       vmx_setup_user_return_msrs();\n+#ifndef __PKVM_HYP__\n+       if (!enable_pkvm)\n+#endif\n+               vmx_setup_user_return_msrs();\n \n \n        if (boot_cpu_has(X86_FEATURE_NX))\n```\n?\n\nIf so then it will never register `kvm_uret_msrs_list` for the host KVM (it will be registered only for pKVM-low). And then it will e.g. trigger this warning:\n```\n[    0.857554] ------------[ cut here ]------------\n[    0.858382] WARNING: CPU: 0 PID: 1 at arch/x86/kvm/cpuid.c:1324 kvm_set_cpu_caps+0x1019/0x10a0\n\n```\nsince `kvm_set_cpu_caps()` explicitly verifies `!kvm_is_supported_user_return_msr(MSR_TSC_AUX)`",
      "parentUuid": "88f835dc_e09dee53",
      "revId": "a33471f42130f67e0c257bf91646f854a31aec54",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
