        "id": 4085392
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-29T01:45:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Or maybe just check `pkvm_cpu_initialized`? If not initialized yet, then we just directly write the value to these MSRs?\n\nIf yes, means uret MSRs are registered in the pKVM and the slot should not be a negative value, and we can BUG_ON in this case.\n\nBTW, as this can happen before sending enable_virtualization_cpu hypercall, the per_cpu `user_return_msrs` is not initialized yet, with all 0 values. But it should be fine for us to use `kvm_set_user_return_msr` here to write these MSRs.",
      "parentUuid": "de1467ca_ba226a16",
      "revId": "a33471f42130f67e0c257bf91646f854a31aec54",
