        "id": 3484945
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-29T11:16:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not sure I follow: I think what we currently have should be ok.\n\n\u003e ...  then maybe just add BUG_ON(!pkvm_cpu_initialized()) here, for extra safety?\n\nThis shouldn\u0027t happen AFAIU: `pkvm_init` which sets `cpu_initialized` happens after de-privileging. And before de-privileging any wrmsrq will not cause the trap and vm exit. Therefore `handle_write_msr` will not be triggered before `pkvm_cpu_initialized` is true so I do not see a reason for this BUG_ON.\n\nFor using `kvm_set_user_return_msr` vs direct write: why should we care and not perform `kvm_set_user_return_msr` unconditionally? I mean:\n- `kvm_uret_msrs_list[]` was already populated globally during hypervisor boot (vmx_hardware_setup()), so slot \u003e\u003d 0 is guaranteed.\n- `kvm_set_user_return_msr(slot, val, -1ull)` writes val to physical hardware and updates .curr \u003d val.\n\nSo keeping simply `BUG_ON(slot \u003c 0);` followed by `kvm_set_user_return_msr(slot, val, -1ull)` seems ok, right? Or I miss some point?",
      "parentUuid": "bf59ef70_74b9400d",
      "revId": "a33471f42130f67e0c257bf91646f854a31aec54",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a293f7e4_a097677f",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/vmx/host_vmx.c",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 214,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-29T11:33:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e This shouldn\u0027t happen AFAIU: pkvm_init which sets cpu_initialized happens after de-privileging. And before de-privileging any wrmsrq will not cause the trap and vm exit. Therefore handle_write_msr will not be triggered before pkvm_cpu_initialized is true so I do not see a reason for this BUG_ON.\n\nThere is a window between the CPU deprivileging (i.e. when the CPU starts running in VMX non-root) and setting `pkvm_cpu_initialized`. During this window, this may happen. (But this _should not_ happen if the still-trusted host behaves as we expect it to, hence the BUG_ON, not just an `if`.)\n\n\u003e For using kvm_set_user_return_msr vs direct write: why should we care and not perform kvm_set_user_return_msr unconditionally? [...]\n\nAt the moment I\u0027m actually thinking it would be good to avoid the need to perform `kvm_set_user_return_msr` at all (because there is no objective need to allow the host to _change_ the values of these MSRs, - because the very idea of user-return MSRs assumes that kernel never needs to change them).",
      "parentUuid": "ec839fb2_e51768a2",
      "revId": "a33471f42130f67e0c257bf91646f854a31aec54",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "35cd4564_3ae9e1c5",
