      "writtenOn": "2026-07-29T12:04:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, now I\u0027m thinking: any actual reason we need to postpone `kvm_user_return_msr_cpu_online()` until the `enable_virtualization_cpu` hypercall? Can\u0027t we do it already in `pkvm_init()` (i.e. as a part of handling the `__pkvm__init` hypercall, on each CPU, before setting its `cpu_initialized`)?\n\nIf we can, then here we can just do this:\n```\n\t\tint slot;\n\t\tu64 cur;\n\t\t\n\t\tBUG_ON(!pkvm_cpu_initialized());\n\n\t\tslot \u003d kvm_find_user_return_msr(msr);\n\t\tBUG_ON(slot \u003c 0);\n\t\tcur \u003d kvm_get_user_return_msr(slot);\n\t\tif (val !\u003d cur) {\n\t\t\tpkvm_warn(\"Host attempt to modify user-return MSR 0x%lx: 0x%llx (expected 0x%llx)\\n\",\n\t\t\t\t  msr, val, cur);\n\t\t\tret \u003d X86EMUL_UNHANDLEABLE;\n\t\t\tbreak;\n\t\t}\n\t\tif (wrmsr_safe(msr, low, high)) {\t/* BTW do we really need this (here and in aosp/4175819)? */\n\t\t\tret \u003d X86EMUL_UNHANDLEABLE;\n\t\t\tbreak;\n\t\t}\n```\n?",
      "parentUuid": "a293f7e4_a097677f",
      "revId": "a33471f42130f67e0c257bf91646f854a31aec54",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
