      "writtenOn": "2026-07-29T13:27:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003eSo, now I\u0027m thinking: any actual reason we need to postpone kvm_user_return_msr_cpu_online() until the enable_virtualization_cpu hypercall? Can\u0027t we do it already in pkvm_init() (i.e. as a part of handling the __pkvm__init hypercall, on each CPU, before setting its cpu_initialized)?\n\nCall `kvm_user_return_msr_cpu_online()` until enable_virtualization_cpu hypercall is just following the KVM. I think we can do this earlier during handling __pkvm_init hypercall. Then we don\u0027t need https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/kernel/common/+/4198684/1?\n\nSeems even with this, there is still a window that, host modify these MSRs before sending the __pkvm_init hypercall? Since the normal host won\u0027t modify these MSRs in this window, I am fine we just add BUG_ON here to simplify the logic.\n\nBTW, this makes me thinking that, maybe in the future, we can refactor the code to setup the MSR bitmap during handling __pkvm_init as well, so that, the host is allowed to directly access the MSRs until pkvm initialized the CPU, which can close this window.",
      "parentUuid": "35cd4564_3ae9e1c5",
