      "writtenOn": "2026-07-29T07:02:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That is interesting observation. Nevertheless I think it is still ok.\n\n\u003e Do we need to add MSR_EFER here? \n\nIf we remove MSR_EFER here, we will not intercept it and allow the host to overwrite MSR_EFER behind pKVM\u0027s back without updating the .curr as this patch cares about.\n\n\u003e Based on my limited understanding we enable VM_ENTRY_LOAD_IA32_EFER, VM_EXIT_SAVE_IA32_EFER and VM_EXIT_LOAD_IA32_EFER so pkvm saves host EFER and loads hyp EFER on VEMXIT and loads the saved host EFER back on VMENTRY.\n\nYou are right but AFAIK:\n- `vmx_setup_user_return_msrs` calls `kvm_add_user_return_msr` for MSR_EFER unconditionally and therefore `kvm_probe_user_return_msr` (which triggers an unconditional wrmsrq, not dependent on `VM_ENTRY_LOAD_IA32_EFER`, `VM_EXIT_SAVE_IA32_EFER` and `VM_EXIT_LOAD_IA32_EFER` wrmsrq). Also  `kvm_add_user_return_msr` adds it to `kvm_uret_msrs_list`. So this write seem legit.\n- Because hardware handles the switch automatically (instructed by `VM_ENTRY_LOAD_IA32_EFER`, `VM_EXIT_SAVE_IA32_EFER` and `VM_EXIT_LOAD_IA32_EFER`), `vmx_prepare_switch_to_guest` checks `!vmx-\u003eguest_uret_msrs[i].load_into_hardware` and skips `kvm_set_user_return_msr` and therefore skips manual switch.",
