      "writtenOn": "2026-07-29T09:40:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e If we remove MSR_EFER here, we will not intercept it and allow the host to overwrite MSR_EFER behind pKVM\u0027s back without updating the .curr as this patch cares about.\n\nBut VM_EXIT_LOAD_IA32_EFER ensures that the EFER value seen by the hypervisor (and, in particular, used by the hypervisor when deciding whether need to write guest\u0027s EFER value) is the EFER value captured during deprivileging (and programmed in the host VMCS via `vmcs_write64(HOST_IA32_EFER, msrq)`), unaffected the host\u0027s writes to EFER (as those writes only affect the value represented by GUEST_IA32_EFER in the host VMCS)?\n\n...That said, I\u0027m not sure I clearly understand yet what exactly happens to EFER across all these host/hyp and hyp/guest switches and why exactly the original KVM code does what it does with EFER. (I think we\u0027d better clearly understand that before merging this.)",
      "parentUuid": "f19c6b26_411d20a5",
