      "message": "\u003e GUEST_IA32_EFER is not updated and is the old value A\n\nI think GUEST_IA32_EFER is updated even earlier, by HW during vmexit, due to VM_EXIT_SAVE_IA32_EFER.\n\n\u003e I think linux doesn\u0027t update MSR_EFER after deprivilege, so should not be an issue.\n\nPer above, it seems it should not be an issue either way.\n\nBut as I wrote in other comments, I think we don\u0027t need to allow the host to modify _any_ user-return MSRs, anyway.\n\n...BTW this makes me wonder: would it be possible to not enable VM_ENTRY_LOAD_IA32_EFER, VM_EXIT_SAVE_IA32_EFER and VM_EXIT_LOAD_IA32_EFER (thus make host vmexits cheaper) and instead rely on intercepting host writes to EFER for preventing the host from modifying it? @chuanxiao.dong@intel.corp-partner.google.com what do you think?",
